From: squadai-stable <noreply@local>
Date: 2026-06-20
Subject: [PATCH] R4 gate (0032) — confine the diagnostic/telemetry paths to the eGPU

Companion to Patch 0031. 0031 gated every *active* recovery lever on
os_pci_is_egpu_target(), and the live B2 test (2026-06-19, driver aorus13)
confirmed R3+R4: under CUDA load the eGPU dropped (Xid 154 on b4:00.0) while
the internal dGPU (10de:2c39 @ 01:00.0) stayed pristine and the PC never froze.

But three *diagnostic* paths were left ungated and still fire on the wrong
device — visible as dmesg noise over the GPU R4 says we must never touch:

  1. nv-lever-m-recover.c tb_egpu_lever_m_close_path_diag() (Patch 0029):
     the char-dev close marker emits "NVRM: GPU 0000:01:00.0: AORUS Lever
     M-recover [CLOSE]" on the INTERNAL dGPU's closes too.
  2. nv-pci.c nv_pci_mmio_enabled / nv_pci_cor_error_detected (Patch 0029):
     dump AER/DIAG on any device's AER callback, internal included.
  3. nvidia-uvm/uvm.c aorus_uvm_*  (Patch 0030): looked up the GPU via a
     HARDCODED BDF 0000:04:00.0 — copied from the single-GPU Fedora reference
     box. On this ThinkPad 0000:04:00.0 is the Samsung NVMe (BAR0 0x92200000),
     so every [UVM-DIAG]/Mode-B Trigger dump was ioremap+ioread32'ing NVMe
     registers and printing them as garbage GPU state (PMC_BOOT_0=0x28033fff,
     WPR2=0xffffffff, pdev=0000:04:00.0). Harmless (read-only) but wrong,
     misleading, and a needless cross-device MMIO poke on every UVM open/close.

Fix — reuse the single-source R4 predicate everywhere:

  - nv-lever-m-recover.c: export a plain-C wrapper tb_egpu_pci_is_egpu_target()
    (takes struct pci_dev * directly) so nvidia-uvm.ko can call the predicate
    without the NV_API_CALL ABI. This TU already pulls in <linux/module.h>
    (EXPORT_SYMBOL) and os-interface.h (os_pci_is_egpu_target, via 0031).
  - tb_egpu_lever_m_close_path_diag(): early-return for non-eGPU.
  - nv_pci_mmio_enabled / nv_pci_cor_error_detected: early-return for non-eGPU
    (mmio_enabled still returns RECOVERED, the prior no-op result).
  - uvm.c: replace the hardcoded-BDF lookup with a topology lookup that walks
    NVIDIA devices and returns the one matching the eGPU predicate (NULL when
    the eGPU is absent), and gate the whole UVM close-path diag on it — so the
    path emits nothing and touches nothing when no eGPU is present.

Net: with the eGPU absent (or for the internal dGPU) the driver is silent on
these paths; with the eGPU present they instrument the eGPU correctly.

NOTE: prepared 2026-06-20, NOT yet built/installed (installed driver is still
aorus13 = patches 0001-0031). This bumps the package to aorus14; build with
`make egpu-dkms`, review with dpkg-deb -c/-I, install, reboot, then re-run the
R3 load test to confirm the dmesg noise is gone and R3+R4 still hold. Because
the patch was authored against reconstructed post-0031 source (the upstream
tree is cloned at build time, not checked in), VERIFY `git apply` succeeds in
the build before relying on it.
---
diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-lever-m-recover.c b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-lever-m-recover.c
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-lever-m-recover.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-lever-m-recover.c
@@ -186,6 +186,18 @@ void tb_egpu_lever_m_diag_dump_pdev(struct pci_dev *pdev, const char *site)
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(tb_egpu_lever_m_diag_dump_pdev);

+/* AORUS Patch 0032 (2026-06-20): plain-C exported wrapper around the R4
+ * predicate so cross-module callers (nvidia-uvm.ko) can confine their
+ * close-path instrumentation to the external eGPU without pulling in the
+ * NV_API_CALL ABI. os_pci_is_egpu_target() is declared via os-interface.h
+ * (included by Patch 0031) and defined in os-pci.c. */
+int tb_egpu_pci_is_egpu_target(struct pci_dev *pdev)
+{
+    return os_pci_is_egpu_target((void *)pdev) ? 1 : 0;
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL(tb_egpu_pci_is_egpu_target);
+
 /* Commit 2: probe-time WPR2-stuck detection.
  *
  * Reads the GSP MMU WPR2 status register via a temporary ioremap of a
@@ -1199,6 +1211,13 @@ void tb_egpu_lever_m_close_path_diag(nv_linux_state_t *nvl,

     if (!nvl)
         return;
+
+    /* AORUS Patch 0032 (2026-06-20): confine the close-path [CLOSE] diag to
+     * the external eGPU. Without this the marker fires on the internal dGPU's
+     * char-dev closes too (GPU 0000:01:00.0), spamming dmesg over the GPU that
+     * R4 says must never be touched. */
+    if (!os_pci_is_egpu_target(nvl->pci_dev))
+        return;

     nv = NV_STATE_PTR(nvl);

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-pci.c b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-pci.c
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-pci.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-pci.c
@@ -2956,6 +2956,10 @@ static pci_ers_result_t nv_pci_mmio_enabled(struct pci_dev *pci_dev)
 {
     nv_linux_state_t *nvl = pci_get_drvdata(pci_dev);

+    /* AORUS Patch 0032 (2026-06-20): only instrument the eGPU; for the
+     * internal dGPU (or any non-eGPU) return the prior no-op result. */
+    if (!os_pci_is_egpu_target(pci_dev))
+        return PCI_ERS_RESULT_RECOVERED;
+
     nv_printf(NV_DBG_ERRORS,
               "AORUS Lever M-recover: mmio_enabled callback fired on %s\n",
               pci_name(pci_dev));
@@ -2982,6 +2986,10 @@ static void nv_pci_cor_error_detected(struct pci_dev *pci_dev)
 {
+    /* AORUS Patch 0032 (2026-06-20): only instrument the eGPU; never dump on
+     * the internal dGPU's correctable-AER callbacks. */
+    if (!os_pci_is_egpu_target(pci_dev))
+        return;
+
     nv_printf(NV_DBG_ERRORS,
               "AORUS Lever M-recover: cor_error_detected callback fired on %s\n",
               pci_name(pci_dev));
diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-uvm/uvm.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-uvm/uvm.c
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-uvm/uvm.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-uvm/uvm.c
@@ -208,6 +208,7 @@
 #include <linux/pci.h>
 #include <linux/atomic.h>
 extern void tb_egpu_lever_m_diag_dump_pdev(struct pci_dev *pdev, const char *site);
 extern void tb_egpu_dump_aer_trigger_event(struct pci_dev *gpu_pdev,
                                           const char *trigger,
                                           void *out);
+extern int  tb_egpu_pci_is_egpu_target(struct pci_dev *pdev);  /* Patch 0032 */

 /* Global UVM fd refcount — incremented in uvm_open, decremented in
  * uvm_release. LAST-CLOSE detection: when the post-decrement value is 0,
@@ -220,12 +221,18 @@ static atomic_t aorus_uvm_fd_count = ATOMIC_INIT(0);

-/* Look up the GPU's pci_dev. Hardcoded BDF 0000:04:00.0 per project
- * topology (only NVIDIA device on this host). Returns NULL if absent.
- * Caller does NOT need to pci_dev_put — pci_get_domain_bus_and_slot
- * increments refcount but for our DIAG snapshot use we only need the
- * pointer momentarily. We pci_dev_put after each use to be safe. */
+/* AORUS Patch 0032 (2026-06-20): look up the EXTERNAL eGPU's pci_dev by
+ * topology instead of the hardcoded BDF 0000:04:00.0 (which on this dual-GPU
+ * ThinkPad is the Samsung NVMe, not a GPU — Patch 0030's dump was reading
+ * NVMe registers as garbage GPU state). Walk NVIDIA devices and return the
+ * first that satisfies the R4 eGPU predicate. Returns NULL when the eGPU is
+ * absent, so the close-path diag below stays silent and never touches the
+ * internal dGPU or the NVMe. Returned device has its refcount held;
+ * caller pci_dev_put()s it. */
 static struct pci_dev *aorus_uvm_get_gpu_pdev(void)
 {
-    return pci_get_domain_bus_and_slot(0, 0x04, PCI_DEVFN(0, 0));
+    struct pci_dev *pdev = NULL;
+    while ((pdev = pci_get_device(0x10de, PCI_ANY_ID, pdev)) != NULL) {
+        if (tb_egpu_pci_is_egpu_target(pdev))
+            return pdev;
+    }
+    return NULL;
 }

-/* DIAG marker — always emits a one-line log with site + fd_count.
- * On is_last_close (post-decrement count==0 OR pre-increment count==0),
- * additionally calls the pdev-based DIAG dump and AER snapshot. */
+/* AORUS Patch 0032 (2026-06-20): DIAG marker, confined to the eGPU.
+ * Looks up the external eGPU first; if absent, emits nothing and touches
+ * nothing. When present, emits the one-line marker and, on is_last_close,
+ * the full pdev-based DIAG dump + AER snapshot on the eGPU. */
 static void aorus_uvm_close_path_diag(const char *site, int fd_count, bool is_last_close)
 {
     struct pci_dev *pdev;

-    pr_info("AORUS UVM [CLOSE]: site=%-18s fd_count=%d%s\n",
-            site, fd_count, is_last_close ? " (LAST-CLOSE)" : "");
-
-    if (is_last_close) {
-        pdev = aorus_uvm_get_gpu_pdev();
-        if (pdev) {
-            tb_egpu_lever_m_diag_dump_pdev(pdev, site);
-            tb_egpu_dump_aer_trigger_event(pdev, site, NULL);
-            pci_dev_put(pdev);
-        } else {
-            pr_info("AORUS UVM [CLOSE]: site=%s — no pdev for 0000:04:00.0; skipping DIAG\n",
-                    site);
-        }
-    }
+    pdev = aorus_uvm_get_gpu_pdev();
+    if (!pdev)
+        return;   /* no eGPU -> no UVM instrumentation at all */
+
+    pr_info("AORUS UVM [CLOSE]: site=%-18s fd_count=%d%s\n",
+            site, fd_count, is_last_close ? " (LAST-CLOSE)" : "");
+
+    if (is_last_close) {
+        tb_egpu_lever_m_diag_dump_pdev(pdev, site);
+        tb_egpu_dump_aer_trigger_event(pdev, site, NULL);
+    }
+
+    pci_dev_put(pdev);
 }
